how to use TPUs, which

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.840
are Tensor Processing Units.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.830
They're Google's own version
of hardware accelerators.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.930
They were designed
and built specifically

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:49.690
to run most efficiently
in Google data centers.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.780
There's a series of four
labs that were created

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.420
by our colleague Martin Gurner.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.410
You can run them
independently or in sequence.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.750
They're a way to run through
some deep learning exercises.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.510
And you don't have to know
anything about deep learning.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.000
Martin is very well known
for doing deep learning

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.070
without a PhD series,
and these labs

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.780
are a great
introduction into that.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.590
But they run on
code lab notebooks,

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.080
which give you all of the
hardware that you need.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.160
They give you access
to everything.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.510
